    "created_at": "2021-04-13T22:57:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-13T22:57:29Z",
    "body": "The bug you're seeing is usually caused by a mismatch in the character-widths between your terminal emulator and shell.\r\nYou can check by removing emoji or other ambiguous-width characters from your prompt, and seeing if it still behaves strangely.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest trying to tweak these iTerm text settings in \"Preferences > Profiles > Text\":\r\n- Use Unicode Version 9 Widths\r\n- Treat ambiguous-width characters as double width\r\n- Unicode normalization form\r\n\r\nIf you still run into issues, try running the following in fish:\r\n```fish\r\nset -g fish_emoji_width 2\r\n```",
